      "writtenOn": "2023-12-08T13:27:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Here\u0027s how I understand things\nskparagraph/src/TextLine.cpp calls `SkShaper::MakeShapeDontWrapOrReorder` (which is only supported by the *harfbuzz* version of SkShaper).\n`skshaper/src/SkShaper_harfbuzz.cpp` calls `SkShaper::Make()`, which could be one of several implementations.\n\nWe would see the same linker problem as having a SkFontMgr factory if we tried to have the client do\n\n```\ncc_binary(\n  ...\n  deps \u003d [\n    \"@skia:skparagraph\",\n    \"@skia:skshaper_harfbuzz\",\n    \"@skia:skunicode_icu\",\n  ]\n)\n```\nAs written, `skparagraph` depends on `skshaper` and `skunicode` so it would need to list those exact dependencies and not trust the client to dep on those for it. Additionally, because `skparagraph` has #ifdefs in it related to skshaper and skunicode, it needs to depend on those modules to have the defines set correctly.\n\nTo solve this, a client of `skparagraph` would need to provide an skshaper factory, which also needs an skunicode factory (or a pre-made instance of skunicode like `SkShaper::MakeShapeDontWrapOrReorder` already does). I believe we would need to remove many (all?) #ifdefs from skparagraph, skshaper, and skunicode, as well.\n\nMaybe this isn\u0027t as complicated as I initially thought, but still a fair bit of work.",
      "parentUuid": "7b9e255a_3221e9f8",
      "revId": "a412767b3e1ef0274097a55a0908c1108e380611",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
